 "_t7/out/cors": "page origin: http://127.0.0.1:<port>   api: http://localhost:<port>  (different host and port ⇒ different origins)\n\n> fetch(api + '/nocors')   — the API sends no CORS header\n  JavaScript got: TypeError: Failed to fetch\n  server saw: GET /nocors  (Origin: http://127.0.0.1:<port>)\n  console: Access to fetch at '<api>/nocors' from origin '<page origin>' has been blocked by CORS policy: No 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header is present on the requested resource.\n  console: Failed to load resource: net::ERR_FAILED\n\n> fetch(api + '/cors')     — Access-Control-Allow-Origin: <page origin>\n  JavaScript got: status 200, body {\"products\":3}\n  server saw: GET /cors  (Origin: http://127.0.0.1:<port>)\n\n> fetch(api + '/no-preflight', { method: 'PUT', JSON body }) — OPTIONS answered without permission\n  JavaScript got: TypeError: Failed to fetch\n  server saw: OPTIONS /no-preflight  (Origin: http://127.0.0.1:<port>)\n  console: Access to fetch at '<api>/no-preflight' from origin '<page origin>' has been blocked by CORS policy: Response to preflight request doesn't pass access control check: No 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header is present on the requested resource.\n  console: Failed to load resource: net::ERR_FAILED\n\n> fetch(api + '/products/2', { method: 'PUT', JSON body }) — preflight allowed\n  JavaScript got: status 200, body {\"updated\":true}\n  server saw: OPTIONS /products/2  (Origin: http://127.0.0.1:<port>)\n  server saw: PUT /products/2  (Origin: http://127.0.0.1:<port>)\n\n> fetch(api + '/star', { credentials: 'include' }) — Allow-Origin: *\n  JavaScript got: TypeError: Failed to fetch\n  server saw: GET /star  (Origin: http://127.0.0.1:<port>)\n  console: Access to fetch at '<api>/star' from origin '<page origin>' has been blocked by CORS policy: The value of the 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header in the response must not be the wildcard '*' when the request's credentials mode is 'include'.\n  console: Failed to load resource: net::ERR_FAILED\n\n> fetch(api + '/creds', { credentials: 'include' }) — exact origin + Allow-Credentials: true\n  JavaScript got: status 200, body {\"ok\":true}\n  server saw: GET /creds  (Origin: http://127.0.0.1:<port>)",
 "_t7/out/csrf": "--- session cookie with SameSite=Lax ---\nAn is logged in at http://localhost:3457, then opens http://127.0.0.1:<port>/ (a different site).\nThe page auto-submits <form method=\"post\" action=\"http://localhost:3457/api/transfer\">.\nServer log:\n  POST /api/transfer (no cookie)\nResponse shown to An: {\"error\":\"Log in first\"}\n\n--- session cookie with SameSite=None; Secure ---\nAn is logged in at http://localhost:3457, then opens http://127.0.0.1:<port>/ (a different site).\nThe page auto-submits <form method=\"post\" action=\"http://localhost:3457/api/transfer\">.\nServer log:\n  POST /api/transfer cookie: sid=…\n  → TRANSFER 5000000 to attacker from An's account\nResponse shown to An: {\"ok\":true,\"from\":\"An\",\"to\":\"attacker\",\"amount\":\"5000000\"}",
 "_t7/out/forgets": "$ curl -s -i -X POST http://localhost:3457/login -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"email\":\"an@example.com\",\"password\":\"correct horse battery\"}'\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\nContent-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8\nSet-Cookie: sid=mrV-d3w22aPoRHPsMdMBtjZrvvCjfqTg3fAfyH0QaMw; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/; Max-Age=3600\n\n{\"name\":\"An\"}\n\n$ curl -s -i http://localhost:3457/api/me\nHTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized\nContent-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8\n\n{\"error\":\"Log in first\"}",
 "_t7/out/httponly": "login → 200\nfetch /api/me → {\"id\":1,\"name\":\"An\",\"role\":\"user\"}   ← the browser attached the HttpOnly cookie\ndocument.cookie → \"theme=dark\"   ← sid is not visible\nlocalStorage.token → \"eyJhbGciOi…(a JWT kept in localStorage)\"\n\nThe browser's cookie store for localhost:\nsid  httpOnly=true  sameSite=Lax  path=/\ntheme  httpOnly=false  sameSite=Lax  path=/",
 "_t7/out/https-bad": "$ curl -sS https://expired.badssl.com/ -o /dev/null; echo \"exit code $?\"\ncurl: (60) SSL certificate problem: certificate has expired\nMore details here: https://curl.se/docs/sslcerts.html\n\ncurl failed to verify the legitimacy of the server and therefore could not\nestablish a secure connection to it. To learn more about this situation and\nhow to fix it, please visit the web page mentioned above.\nexit code 60\n\n$ curl -sS https://self-signed.badssl.com/ -o /dev/null; echo \"exit code $?\"\ncurl: (60) SSL certificate problem: self signed certificate\nMore details here: https://curl.se/docs/sslcerts.html\n\ncurl failed to verify the legitimacy of the server and therefore could not\nestablish a secure connection to it. To learn more about this situation and\nhow to fix it, please visit the web page mentioned above.\nexit code 60",
 "_t7/out/https-ok": "$ curl -sv https://example.com/ -o /dev/null 2>&1 | grep -E \"TLS|SSL|ALPN|subject|issuer|expire|start date\"   (lines filtered)\n* ALPN: curl offers h2,http/1.1\n* (304) (OUT), TLS handshake, Client hello (1):\n* (304) (IN), TLS handshake, Server hello (2):\n* (304) (IN), TLS handshake, Unknown (8):\n* (304) (IN), TLS handshake, Finished (20):\n* (304) (OUT), TLS handshake, Finished (20):\n* SSL connection using TLSv1.3 / AEAD-CHACHA20-POLY1305-SHA256 / [blank] / UNDEF\n* ALPN: server accepted h2\n*  subject: CN=example.com\n*  start date: Sep 26 22:49:11 2026 GMT\n*  expire date: Dec 25 22:56:35 2026 GMT\n*  subjectAltName: host \"example.com\" matched cert's \"example.com\"\n*  issuer: C=US; O=SSL Corporation; CN=Cloudflare TLS Issuing ECC CA 3\n*  SSL certificate verify ok.",
